      ],
      "spread_K": 2.26,
      "verdict": "Does NOT generalize cross-volcano. Optimal cut is regime/volcano-dependent (focal centers higher 4-5K, nevado lower 2.8-3.9K). A single global physical threshold cannot separate both regimes cleanly."
    },
    "within_nevado_failure": "Within the nevado regime test1_k AUC drops to 0.762 and the rare real signals (Llaima n=1, Copahue n=4, Villarrica n=18) overlap with artifact: there is no faint-signal floor that distinguishes real lava-lake/dome cat-b from topographic artifact at the same energy."
  },
  "conclusion": {
    "clean_physical_cut_exists": false,
    "summary": "No single non-geometric PHYSICAL discriminant separates cat-b real from nevado artifact at >80%/>80%. The best candidate (test1_k_observed, AUC 0.859) is regime-dependent (per-vol cut 2.76-5.02K) and any global cut that rejects >70% nevado artifact also destroys 14-16% of confirmed cat-b real (faint sub-pixel = A54/A82 the protected value). nti_max (A80) is refuted (AUC 0.251). The fundamental physics (A82): faint real foci in snow and the diffuse topographic artifact are spectrally/energetically the SAME object per-record; only the SPATIAL/temporal-context dimension separates them.",
    "recommendation": "Confirms the C2 conclusion: the clean separator is NOT a per-record physical scalar. Either the geometric gate (distance) or a per-volcano/per-regime approach remains the only viable path. A physical discriminant could only work stratified by regime (focal cut ~4-5K vs nevado), which is operationally a per-volcano gate dressed as physics."
  }
